    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.splitjoin\n\n### Description\n\nIt would be nice to be able to turn on hanging indents on split join in Python, i.e.:\r\n```python\r\ni = [1, 2, 3]\r\n\r\n# mini.splitjoin\r\n\r\ni = [\r\n    1,\r\n    2,\r\n    3,\r\n    ]\r\n```\r\n\r\nThere was a setting for this in https://github.com/AndrewRadev/splitjoin.vim :\r\n\r\n```vim\r\nvim.g.splitjoin_python_brackets_on_separate_lines = 1\r\n```",
