            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for suggestion!\r\n\r\n'mini.splitjoin' can be customized with hooks. Something [like this](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/50ade2218c2ad32b1c6421ea500adaad01fa476f/doc/mini-splitjoin.txt#L365-L381). Here is a [starting point](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/50ade2218c2ad32b1c6421ea500adaad01fa476f/doc/mini-splitjoin.txt#L211) to read about them. It is not planned to have such specific options as you mentioned, unfortunately.\r\n\r\nWould you mind clarifying what exactly you mean here? I might be able to help you set this up. Preferably with example of \"before\" and \"after\".",
