        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "So if I understand correctly, you want to also increase indent of last line (along with other inner ones). Here is the post split hook for that:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nlocal hang_indent = function(split_positions)\r\n  -- Increase indent of the last split\r\n  local last_split = split_positions[#split_positions]\r\n  local line, col = last_split.line - 1, last_split.col - 1\r\n  local pad = vim.bo.expandtab and string.rep(' ', vim.fn.shiftwidth()) or '\\t'\r\n  vim.api.nvim_buf_set_text(0, line, col, line, col, { pad })\r\nend\r\n```\r\n\r\nIf you want this only for square brackets, here is possible solution:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nlocal hang_indent = function(split_positions)\r\n  -- Increase indent of the last split only inside square brackets \r\n  local last_split = split_positions[#split_positions]\r\n  local line, col = last_split.line - 1, last_split.col - 1\r\n\r\n  local is_square = vim.fn.getline(line + 1):sub(col + 1, col + 1) == ']'\r\n  if not is_square then return end\r\n\r\n  local pad = vim.bo.expandtab and string.rep(' ', vim.fn.shiftwidth()) or '\\t'\r\n  vim.api.nvim_buf_set_text(0, line, col, line, col, { pad })\r\nend\r\n```\r\n\r\nIf you want to use this only for Python, I'd recommend creating 'after/ftplugin/python.lua' file with the following code:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nif _G.MiniSplitjoin ~= nil then\r\n  local hang_indent = function(split_positions)\r\n    -- Enter code which you prefer\r\n  end\r\n\r\n  vim.b.minisplitjoin_config = { split = { hooks_post = { hang_indent } } }\r\nend\r\n```\r\n\r\nIf you want this globally, set this config inside `require('mini.splitjion').setup()`.\r\n\r\nDoes this solve your problem?",
